---
import Site from "../../layouts/Site.astro";

/**
 * The privacy notice for the Mzizi surfaces. Every statement here is one this
 * repository, the API, the MCP server or the Bundu Foundation's and Nyuchi's own
 * notices can back: what the site loads, what the read-only API stores (nothing),
 * what the MCP server does with a sign-in and an issue report. Do not add a data
 * practice here that the code does not have, and change this page in the same
 * pull request as the change that alters one. The date below is the last time the
 * facts were checked against the code.
 */
const UPDATED = "12 November 2026";
---

<Site
  title="Privacy"
  description="What the Mzizi websites, API, MCP server and Claude plugin collect, and where the Bundu Foundation's and Nyuchi's notices apply."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lede={`Last updated ${UPDATED}. What mzizi.dev, docs.mzizi.dev, api.mzizi.dev, mcp.mzizi.dev and the Mzizi Claude plugin collect, and who to ask.`}
>
  <h2>Who this covers</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    This notice covers the Mzizi surfaces that are public and free to read:{" "}
    <code>mzizi.dev</code>, <code>docs.mzizi.dev</code>, <code>api.mzizi.dev</code>,{" "}
    <code>mcp.mzizi.dev</code> and the Mzizi Claude plugin. Mzizi is not a separate legal
    entity. It sits inside the Bundu ecosystem, whose parent is the Bundu Foundation, a
    non-profit company limited by guarantee registered in Zimbabwe. The Foundation's{" "}
    <a href="https://www.bundu.org/legal/privacy">privacy notice</a> is the umbrella notice,
    and this page adds what is specific to Mzizi.
  </p>
  <p class="prose">
    The Mzizi console at <code>app.mzizi.dev</code> has accounts. It is run by Nyuchi Africa
    (Pvt) Ltd, and <a href="https://www.nyuchi.com/legal/privacy">Nyuchi's privacy notice</a>{" "}
    governs it.
  </p>

  <h2>What each surface collects</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>mzizi.dev.</strong> A static site. It has no accounts, sets no cookies, and runs
      no analytics or advertising scripts. Search runs in your browser, over files the site
      serves. Your browser asks Google Fonts for the typefaces, so Google sees your IP address
      and the page that asked.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>api.mzizi.dev.</strong> A read-only API that answers from files bundled when it was
      built. It has no database and no accounts, so it keeps nothing about who asked.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>mcp.mzizi.dev.</strong> The Mzizi MCP server. The free tools need no sign-in. It
      limits requests per IP address, so it reads your address to do that. Two tools,{" "}
      <code>mzizi_fundi</code> and <code>mzizi_report_issue</code>, need you to sign in and act
      as your Mzizi console user. A report you send with <code>mzizi_report_issue</code> is
      recorded in our database and filed as a GitHub issue, so do not put a secret or anyone's
      personal data in one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>docs.mzizi.dev.</strong> Hosted by Mintlify, which processes page requests and may
      collect usage analytics under its own notice.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The Mzizi Claude plugin.</strong> Markdown skills and a connection to the MCP
      server above. It runs no script of its own and sends nothing anywhere else.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    These sites and servers are hosted on Cloudflare, which processes request data (IP address,
    address requested, browser) to deliver and protect them. The other processors are Google
    (Fonts), Mintlify (the documentation) and GitHub (the issues and the source). Nothing here is
    sold, and there is no advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    Depending on where you live you have rights of access, correction, portability, deletion and
    objection, and the right to withdraw consent. The Foundation's notice is drafted to satisfy
    the Zimbabwe Data Protection Act, POPIA and the EU GDPR; this one follows it. Write to{" "}
    <a href="mailto:support@bundu.org">support@bundu.org</a> with the subject line "Data
    request". Security reports go to <a href="mailto:security@nyuchi.com">security@nyuchi.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    A change to what the surfaces collect changes this page, with the date above. The history is
    in this site's <a href="https://github.com/mzizi-dev/mzizi-site/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">changelog</a>.
    See also the <a href="/legal/terms">terms of use</a>.
  </p>
</Site>
